---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Home" description="Heliophysics and Space Weather research group at Universidad de Santiago de Chile. Radiation belts, ULF waves, GIC and machine learning for space weather forecasting." variant="home">

<section class="hp-hero" id="inicio">
  <img src="/images/eso1912u-la-silla-eclipse.jpg" alt="Polarised solar corona during the 2019 total eclipse observed from La Silla" />
  <div class="hp-hero-scrim"></div>
  <div class="hp-hero-content">
    <p class="hp-eyebrow">Universidad de Santiago de Chile — Dept. of Physics</p>
    <h1>Where the Sun ends,<br/>space weather begins.</h1>
    <p class="hp-hero-sub">We study Earth's radiation belts, the waves that shake the magnetosphere, and build artificial intelligence models to forecast their effects on satellites and power grids.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="hp-hero-credit">Polarised solar corona, 2019 La Silla total eclipse — Credit: ESA/CESAR</p>
</section>

<section class="hp-intro hp-reveal">
  <div class="hp-wrap">
    <div class="hp-intro-grid">
      <figure class="hp-intro-figure">
        <img src="/images/eso1703c-alma-solar-disc.jpg" alt="The full solar disc observed by ALMA at millimeter wavelengths" />
        <figcaption>The Sun observed at millimeter wavelengths by ALMA — the same plasma that drives space weather. Credit: ALMA (ESO/NAOJ/NRAO).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="hp-intro-text">
        <p class="hp-lede">Every second, the Sun hurls charged particles and magnetic fields into space that reach Earth minutes to hours later.</p>
        <p>That flow —calm most of the time, violent during a geomagnetic storm— tests satellites, power grids and navigation systems. At USACH's Heliophysics and Space Weather Group we measure, model, and try to anticipate that impact.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-value">14+</div><div class="stat-label">Active projects</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-value">29</div><div class="stat-label">Peer-reviewed papers</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-value">10+</div><div class="stat-label">Students trained</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-value">4</div><div class="stat-label">Collaborating countries</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-value">700+</div><div class="stat-label">Citations</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hp-research" id="investigacion">
  <div class="hp-wrap">
    <div class="hp-section-head hp-reveal">
      <p class="hp-eyebrow">Research lines</p>
      <h2>Three research lines</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="hp-research-grid hp-reveal">
      <article class="hp-research-card">
        <img src="/images/eso1912aa-soho-sdo-lasilla.jpg" alt="Combined image of the Sun and its surroundings from SOHO, SDO and La Silla" />
        <div class="hp-research-body">
          <span class="hp-research-tag">Space physics</span>
          <h3>Radiation belts</h3>
          <p>Relativistic electron energization and decay. Enhancement and dropout events in the outer belt. Formation and evolution of ultrarelativistic remnant belts.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="hp-research-card">
        <img src="/images/eso1912y-solar-corona.jpg" alt="Inner and outer solar corona" />
        <div class="hp-research-body">
          <span class="hp-research-tag">Space physics</span>
          <h3>ULF waves & turbulence</h3>
          <p>Wave-particle interactions in the magnetosphere. Turbulence and total pressure balance. Solar wind—magnetosphere coupling and effects on satellites.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="hp-research-card">
        <img src="/images/eso1912u-la-silla-eclipse.jpg" alt="Polarised solar corona during the 2019 total eclipse" />
        <div class="hp-research-body">
          <span class="hp-research-tag">Data science</span>
          <h3>ML for space weather</h3>
          <p>Prediction of ground magnetic perturbations, geomagnetically induced currents (GIC), and near real-time forecasting models with deep learning.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hp-projects" id="proyectos">
  <div class="hp-wrap">
    <div class="hp-section-head hp-reveal">
      <p class="hp-eyebrow">Projects</p>
      <h2>From basic science to critical infrastructure</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="hp-project-list hp-reveal">
      <article class="hp-project-card featured">
        <div class="hp-project-media">
          <img src="/images/eso1035a-hd10180-system.jpg" alt="Artist's impression of a planetary system, illustrating the group's data-platform work" />
        </div>
        <div class="hp-project-body">
          <p class="hp-project-kicker">FONDEF IDEA I+D — ANID</p>
          <h3>Chilean Space Weather Platform</h3>
          <p>Chile's first national pilot platform for real-time space weather monitoring and early warnings.</p>
          <div class="hp-project-tags">
            <span>Real-time monitoring</span>
            <span>DL predictive models</span>
            <span>HPC platform</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="hp-project-card">
        <div class="hp-project-media">
          <img src="/images/eso1333c-snow-line-alma.jpg" alt="Visualization of ALMA observational data" />
        </div>
        <div class="hp-project-body">
          <p class="hp-project-kicker">FONDEQUIP EQM230160</p>
          <h3>HPC Platform USACH</h3>
          <p>High-performance computing platform for data science, simulations, and numerical modeling.</p>
          <div class="hp-project-tags">
            <span>High-performance computing</span>
            <span>Numerical simulation</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hp-team" id="equipo">
  <div class="hp-wrap">
    <div class="hp-section-head hp-reveal">
      <p class="hp-eyebrow">Team</p>
      <h2>A small, growing team</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="hp-team-grid hp-reveal">
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">VP</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Victor A. Pinto</span>
          <span class="role">Principal investigator</span>
          <span class="bio">Assistant Professor, Dept. of Physics USACH. Ph.D. in Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (Space Physics), UCLA 2019. Radiation belts, ULF waves and machine learning for space weather.</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">MS</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Marina Stepanova</span>
          <span class="role">Co-investigator</span>
          <span class="bio">Associate Professor, Dept. of Physics USACH. Magnetospheric turbulence, relativistic electron dynamics and the space weather platform.</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">AI</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Ana María Inostroza</span>
          <span class="role">Master of Science in Physics, USACH</span>
          <span class="bio">Outer radiation belt dynamics and auroral phenomena.</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">BZ</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Bea Zenteno-Quinteros</span>
          <span class="role">Master of Science in Physics, USACH</span>
          <span class="bio">Relativistic electron loss processes by electromagnetic waves.</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">DM</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Dafhne Muñoz Reyes</span>
          <span class="role">Astrophysics Engineering, USACH</span>
          <span class="bio">ML model for plasmapause location (Van Allen Probes).</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <button class="hp-team-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="initials">CP</span>
        <span class="overlay">
          <span class="name">Camila Peña Cifuentes</span>
          <span class="role">Physics Engineering, USACH</span>
          <span class="bio">Deep Learning prediction of relativistic electron flux.</span>
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <a class="hp-team-more" href="/en/team">See full team →</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hp-publications" id="publicaciones">
  <div class="hp-wrap">
    <div class="hp-section-head hp-reveal">
      <p class="hp-eyebrow">Publications</p>
      <h2>Recent publications</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="hp-pub-list hp-reveal">
      <li class="hp-pub-item">
